# MoOS: this file REPLACES the one plasma-discover-notifier installs at this path.
#
# Discover's notifier is a second updater. It autostarts in every session (measured
# live 2026-09-24: app-org.kde.discover.notifier@autostart.service, active), pops
# "updates available" notices under its own name, and — with the base image's
# UseUnattendedUpdates=true — installs them itself. MoOS already has one update
# authority for the system image (moos-image-update, shown in MoOS Settings → Update)
# and one for applications (uupd), so this one is switched off. Discover's engine
# stays: Mo Store and .flatpakref files still use it.
#
# Hidden=true is the XDG autostart spec's "treat as deleted": systemd's
# xdg-autostart-generator (which Plasma uses to start autostart entries) and
# Plasma's own autostart list both skip the entry. Exec=/bin/true is the second lock.
#
# How an override of a package-owned /etc file behaves in this image:
#   * x86: `COPY system_files/ /` runs after the base already installed the package,
#     so this file replaces the package's; no later build transaction reinstalls it.
#     plasma_seams.py's rpm -V registry covers only plasma-desktop, plasma-workspace,
#     kscreenlocker, kwin, libplasma and plasma-login-manager, so it does not object.
#   * ARM: build-arm.sh copies the overlay again after its package installs (`cp -a
#     /moos-overlay/. /`), so the same bytes win there.
#   * A package update that rewrote this file would be caught: curate_app_menu.sh's
#     gate fails the build unless the notifier's autostart entry is Hidden=true.
#   * On an installed machine /etc is merged three-way by OSTree: a machine whose
#     owner never edited this file takes each new image's version.
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Update notifier (replaced by MoOS)
Name[ar]=منبّه التحديثات (استبدله MoOS)
Exec=/bin/true
Hidden=true
NoDisplay=true
